From b4e5b7566addfaa86a81b84d4f07259d1861c217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ffmpeg: enable crypto protocol for AES-128 HLS

The pinned FFmpeg HLS demuxer wraps AES-128 media segments in a
crypto+<segment URL>. GE configures FFmpeg with --disable-everything and
enables only the HTTPS protocol explicitly, leaving CONFIG_CRYPTO_PROTOCOL
disabled and encrypted HLS unable to open its top-level wrapper.

Enable only the crypto URLProtocol. RTSP-on-GE11 keeps it out of the generic
progressive HTTP allowlists and permits it only through the HLS-specific
allowlists, where crypto.c propagates the same parent whitelist to the nested
HTTP(S) segment URL.

This is a project-authored build integration patch, not an upstream GE patch.
---
 Makefile.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
index 63fa764..a27cd2d 100644
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -310,6 +310,7 @@ FFMPEG_CONFIGURE_ARGS := \
 	--enable-gnutls \
 	--enable-demuxers \
 	--enable-protocol=https \
+	--enable-protocol=crypto \
 	--enable-decoders \
 	--enable-encoders \
 	--enable-bsfs \
